{"parentUuid":"c1a537c9-1d2e-4a3a-9387-9359fce2f304","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a407c19b077d521aa","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_vrtx_011CdrTjhPvnRtaPpkHz8jYg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01BToc31WSWZKik4XF7SfoQ4","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"family":"object","vectorFile":"/workspace/probes/object.jsonl","vectorCount":1314,"findings":"HARNESS (/workspace/dataset/test13.py): validator_class = jsonschema.validators.validator_for(schema); prints validator_class.__name__, then is_valid(instance), then len(list(iter_errors(instance))). Any exception escapes from the is_valid() call, so a crash means exit 1, EMPTY stdout (not even the validator-name line), traceback on stderr.\n\nVALIDATOR SELECTION (NEWLY PROBED — was missing). With NO $schema key at all, validator_for returns Draft202012Validator (verified: {\"a\":\"s\"} + {properties:{a:{type:\"integer\"}}} => \"Draft202012Validator/False/1\"; {x:1}+{unevaluatedProperties:false} => Draft202012Validator/False/1, i.e. 2020-12 semantics including unevaluatedProperties; {a:1}+{dependencies:{a:[\"x\"]}} => Draft202012Validator/True/0, dependencies silently ignored). An UNKNOWN/unrecognized $schema string (e.g. \"http://example.com/unknown\") ALSO falls back to Draft202012Validator (no error, no crash). Recognized ids: draft-03 -> Draft3Validator, draft-04 -> Draft4Validator, draft-06 -> Draft6Validator, draft-07 -> Draft7Validator, 2019-09 -> Draft201909Validator, 2020-12 -> Draft202012Validator.\n\nNON-OBJECT INSTANCES: ALL object keywords are no-ops when the instance is not a JSON object (array, null, string, number, boolean) — verified in every draft with a schema stacking properties+patternProperties+additionalProperties:false+required+minProperties+propertyNames against [1] and null: True/0. Also dependentRequired against [1] => True/0, dependencies against [1] => True/0, propertyNames against [1,2] => True/0, unevaluatedProperties against non-object => 0.\n\nPROPERTIES (all drafts, identical). Each failing (property, keyword) pair yields ONE top-level error. 3 props each failing type => 3. One prop failing two keywords (type+minLength) => 2. Two props each failing two keywords => 4. Nested descent FLATTENS to top level: {\"o\":{\"p\":\"s\",\"q\":\"t\"}} with properties.o.properties.{p,q}:integer => 2; 3-level nesting {\"o\":{\"p\":{\"r\":\"s\",\"t\":\"u\"}}} with two failing leaves => 2; 3-level with one leaf failure => 1. properties entries whose key is absent from the instance are skipped entirely (their subschema is never even looked at — properties:{a:null} with instance {\"b\":1} => 0 errors, no crash). Boolean subschemas: properties:{a:false,b:false} with both present => 2; properties:{a:true} => 0. properties:{} => 0. A key nested inside properties with additionalProperties:false inside => 1 aggregate; with required:[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"] inside => 3.\n  CRASHES: `properties` whose VALUE is not a mapping ({\"properties\":[\"a\"]} or \"a\") => exit 1, AttributeError 'list'/'str' has no attribute 'items' (_keywords.py:294). A properties ENTRY whose subschema is null / string / number / array CRASHES only if that key is PRESENT in the instance (properties:{a:null}, {a:\"x\"}, {a:5}, {a:[]} with {\"a\":1} => exit 1 AttributeError; with the key absent => 0 errors).\n\nPATTERNPROPERTIES (all drafts incl. draft3). Regex is Python re.SEARCH, NOT fullmatch and NOT anchored — pattern \"a\" matches key \"xay\" (1 error). A key matching N patterns is validated against ALL N subschemas and yields N separate top-level errors ({\"abc\":\"s\"} with \"^a\"(integer) and \"c$\"(boolean) => 2; 3 matching failing patterns => 3). Boolean false per matching key: {\"pa\":1,\"pb\":2} with {\"^p\":false} => 2. A key covered by BOTH properties and patternProperties is validated by both ({\"pa\":\"s\"} with properties.pa:integer + patternProperties.\"^p\":boolean => 2). Empty pattern \"\" matches EVERY key ({\"a\":\"s\",\"b\":\"t\"} with {\"\":{type:\"integer\"}} => 2). patternProperties:{} => 0.\n  PYTHON-vs-JS REGEX DIALECT (NEWLY PROBED — the single biggest reimplementation hazard): patterns are compiled with Python `re` in UNICODE mode and applied with re.search.\n   - \"\\\\d\" MATCHES non-ASCII digits: key \"١\" (Arabic-Indic one) matches \"\\\\d\" => 1 error. JS /\\d/ would not match. Same for \"\\\\w\": key \"éx\" matches \"^\\\\w+$\" => 1 error (JS /^\\w+$/ would not).\n   - \"$\" matches BEFORE a trailing newline (Python semantics): key \"a\\n\" matches \"^a$\" => 1 error. JS /^a$/ does not match \"a\\n\". Use \"\\\\Z\" for a true end anchor: key \"a\\n\" does NOT match \"^a\\\\Z\" => 0 errors. (JS has no \\Z; in JS \\Z is just the literal \"Z\".)\n   - \"$\" is still NOT multiline by default: key \"a\\nb\" does NOT match \"^b$\" => 0 errors.\n   - \".\" does not match newline: key \"a\\nb\" vs \"^a.b$\" => 0 errors.\n   - Python inline flags WORK: \"(?i)abc\" matches key \"ABC\" => 1 error. JS throws on \"(?i)\".\n   - Python named groups \"(?P<n>a)b\" WORK (match key \"ab\" => 1 error). JS-style named groups \"(?<n>a)b\" CRASH (exit 1, re.error). Lookbehind \"(?<=x)a\" works (key \"xa\" => 1). Backreference \"(a)\\\\1\" works (key \"aa\" => 1). \"\\\\b\" works (key \"a b\" vs \"\\\\bb\\\\b\" => 1).\n   - \"\\\\p{L}\" CRASHES (exit 1, Python re has no \\p). Empty character class \"[]\" CRASHES (Python treats it as unterminated; JS treats [] as never-match).\n   - Invalid regex is compiled LAZILY, only when there is at least one instance key to test: patternProperties:{\"[\":{...}} with instance {} => True/0 (no crash); with any key present => exit 1 re.error unterminated character set. It also crashes when additionalProperties is present and there is a key, since additionalProperties must run the same regexes ({\"z\":1} + patternProperties:{\"[\":...} + additionalProperties:false => exit 1).\n   - Non-mapping patternProperties (a list) => exit 1 AttributeError ... 'items' (